questions.text:
Which of the following phenomena are explained by interference:
1) the iridescent colors of a thin oil film;
2) the formation of a bright spot at the center of the shadow of a small object;
3) Newton's rings;
4) the bending of light rays into the region of geometric shadow?

Which of the following phenomena are explained by the interference of light:
1) the iridescent colors seen in a soap bubble or an oil film;
2) Newton's rings;
3) the formation of a bright spot at the center of the shadow of a small circular disk;
4) the bending of light rays at the edge of an obstacle into the region of geometric shadow.
